# subarray_sums:
# CSES 1660, Subarray Sums I (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1660), in our own words:
# a list of positive numbers and a target x; the contiguous subarrays, stretches of
# consecutive places, whose numbers sum to x. The input is the binary natural x
# (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and a Scott list
# (corpora/library/prelude/list) of positive binary naturals; the answer is a binary
# natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: every contiguous subarray is built (for each
# place the list is cut at, the nonempty prefixes of what follows), each is summed by
# adding its numbers, and those whose sum is x are counted. Its reading builds about n
# squared / 2 subarrays and sums each; the replacement the family asks for is two
# pointers, which move the right end over each place and the left end right while the
# sum is above x, in about n steps, on fixed-width integers (the numbers being
# positive is what lets the left end only move right).
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion consumes the finite list of
# numbers, of subarrays or of one subarray; the branches that a Scott boolean discards
# are never read. The program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the
# soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14
# (Lean `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while
# Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and
# applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items nil λ head tail. cons (cons head nil) λ. map (cons head) λ. self tail
  )
λ prefixes
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items nil λ _ tail. append (prefixes items) λ. self tail
  )
λ subarrays
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λ self total items. items total λ head tail. self (merge_binary_plus total head) tail
  )
λ sum_of
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ target
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self found subarray_list
        . subarray_list found
          λ subarray rest
          . self (merge_binary_equality (sum_of binary_zero subarray) target (merge_binary_increment found) found) rest
      )
  )
λ with_sum
. (λtuple. tuple λtarget values. with_sum target binary_zero (subarrays values))
λ subarray_sums
. export subarray_sums
